-- title:
--   A uniform polynomial envelope for the complete machine cost
-- statement:
--   For natural $E,P,F,Q\ge1$, define
--   $$\begin{aligned}C={}&16080EPFQ+12000000000000P^2FQ\\&+10008(6144EP^7FQ)+10000P+110330000P^4F\\&+10^{25}EP^{14}FQ+10021.\end{aligned}$$
--   Then
--   $$C\le10^{28}EP^{20}FQ.$$
--   No asymptotic convention is needed for this inequality. In the machine analysis, the intended substitution is $E=2^k$, $P=1+k+n+L$, $F=4^a$, and $Q=b+1$, where $L$ is the graph encoding length. The terms cover parsing, setup, random-bit loading, native estimation, and output overhead. This algebraic lemma assembles their separate bounds into one fixed global time budget.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/WholeCost.lean, line 15; source snapshot SHA-256 bb17fc66db1b5999b87e164401dc2f2c936501b688663f3afc5d55bd64ff16a5.

